---
import ClaimLedger from "../components/ClaimLedger.astro";
import ResearchLayout from "../layouts/ResearchLayout.astro";
import data from "../generated/site-data.json";
const { project, authors, links, results, packages, claims } = data;
const pilotRecall = (results.core_specs_recall * 100).toFixed(1);
---
<ResearchLayout title={project.title} description={project.abstract}>
  <header class="topbar">
    <a href="#top">Product attribute saturation</a>
    <nav aria-label="Primary navigation"><a href="#method">Method</a><a href="#evidence">Evidence</a><a href="#reproduce">Reproduce</a></nav>
  </header>
  <main id="top">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="paper-title">
      <div class="hero__content">
        <p class="article-kicker">Research in progress</p>
        <h1 id="paper-title">{project.title}</h1>
        <p class="subtitle">{project.subtitle}</p>
        <p class="hero-result"><span>Reduced-corpus BM25 pilot · Recall@10</span><strong>{pilotRecall}% with core specifications</strong></p>
        <p class="byline">{authors.map(author => author.name).join(", ")}</p>
        <p class="abstract">{project.abstract}</p>
        <p><a href={links.repository}>Source and experiment protocol</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section section--rule" id="method" aria-labelledby="method-title">
      <h2 id="method-title">One fixed corpus, progressively richer representations</h2>
      <p>Compare {results.representation_levels} cumulative levels: title, identity, variants, core specifications, and all mapped text fields. Each level receives the same ShoppingBench queries and target-product labels. The first pilot uses BM25 and makes no LLM calls.</p>
      <p>Measure Recall@1/5/10, truncated reciprocal rank, and nDCG@5/10. Paired query bootstrap intervals quantify adjacent gains and the earliest level retaining 90%, 95%, or 99% of the best observed score.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="section section--rule" id="evidence" aria-labelledby="evidence-title">
      <h2 id="evidence-title">Pilot results and their limits</h2>
      <p>{results.status}. The archived run uses {results.pilot_queries} queries and {results.pilot_products.toLocaleString("en-US")} products, including every target and hash-sampled distractors. A reduced-corpus run cannot establish full-corpus saturation, and lexical retrieval does not establish LLM selection performance.</p>
      <p>Attribute groups can repeat facts already present in titles or descriptions. The pilot measures field-group enrichment, not a universal count of independent facts. Randomized ordering and full-corpus experiments remain necessary.</p>
      <ClaimLedger claims={claims} />
    </section>
    <section class="section section--materials" id="reproduce" aria-labelledby="reproduce-title">
      <h2 id="reproduce-title">Reproduce the pilot</h2>
      <pre aria-label="Reproduction command"><code>python -m study.run_shoppingbench_pilot \
  --documents /data/documents.jsonl.gz \
  --queries /data/synthesize_product_test.jsonl \
  --output runs/shoppingbench-pilot</code></pre>
      <p>Requires Java 21 and the experiment extra. Every completed run includes input and output hashes, the executed config, query-level metrics, representation sizes, bootstrap analysis, and environment versions.</p>
      <p>Python: {packages.python.distribution}. npm: {packages.javascript.name}. Package conformance fixtures validate infrastructure only.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</ResearchLayout>
